601 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 390 0 R
/T (Low voltage cables can also be supplied with polyethylene over sheath. Polyethylene offers the advantage of much greater impermeability to moisture compared to PVC and can also offer much greater abrasion resistance. These can be important factors when selecting cables for use in hostile environments. All sheaths are designed with easy strip characteristics to further reduce the time and cost of cable preparation and installation. Also, finished cables are marked on their outer sheath to help cable identification on site.)
/E (Low voltage cables can also be supplied with polyethylene over sheath. Polyethylene offers the advantage of much greater impermeability to moisture compared to PVC and can also offer much greater abrasion resistance. These can be important factors when selecting cables for use in hostile environments. All sheaths are designed with easy strip characteristics to further reduce the time and cost of cable preparation and installation. Also, finished cables are marked on their outer sheath to help cable identification on site.)
