/Title (SCC low voltage cables are normally supplied with PVC type ST2 over sheath complying with IEC 60502 , and are colored black. Other colors may be provided to suit a range of installation considerations such as the effect of UV radiations and different soil conditions. Anti-termite formulations can also be supplied as well as graphite- coated over sheath where on-site DC testing of the sheath is required. Please contact our technical department for full details.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 48210 0 R
/Next 48223 0 R
>>
endobj
48223 0 obj
<<
/Title (Low voltage cables can also be supplied with polyethylene over sheath. Polyethylene offers the advantage of much greater impermeability to moisture compared to PVC and can also offer much greater abrasion resistance. These can be important factors when selecting cables for use in hostile environments. All sheaths are designed with easy strip characteristics to further reduce the time and cost of cable preparation and installation. Also, finished cables are marked on their outer sheath to help cable identification on site.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 48210 0 R
/Prev 48222 0 R
>>
